{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1473134-talon-survival-guide","id":1473134,"title":"Talon Survival Guide","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-01-23T20:26:49-08:00","id":1473134,"title":"Talon Survival Guide","content":"So, this thread is intended as a place to debate and document Mage's approach to warfare and combat outside of the Duel Arcane. Spells, tactics, and combat priorities are all welcome. First order of business, discussing the combat capabilities of a practitioner of each of the Arcana. We shall start with Forces, and hopefully work our way through the rest of the Arcana.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1473124#post1473124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A master of Forces can be flying across the battlefield with no problems, whilst invisible and inaudible (cutting off touch spells and making sensory ones difficult). Even if someone finds them, they can turn anything back at the attacker regardless of size, such as sniper bullets or the giant ship container the Life mage tossed at them.<br /> <br /> They can impose radio and physical silence in the area, shroud it in darkness and command all electronic defenses. They can alter gravity to imprison or disorient you, bring down your entire highly defended sanctum down on you with an earthquake (or sonic resonance). They can set an area on fire and fight you unfazed while you choke and burn.<br /> <br /> As a matter of fact, they don't even need to bother being there in person. With their attuned eyes (Nightvision), hearing (Receiver) and absurd long distance vision (Zoom In), they can attack you from the sky in a sensory range measured in miles. If they have Space (to mix the Outward &amp; Inward Eyes into it) or Matter (to see through walls), its becomes a true nightmare.<br /> <br /> Its an Arcanum with a lot of potential for grandiose effects, especially when leveraging existing forces.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main weakness of Forces is lacking power over the less direct and physical. Intangibility, Mental Manipulations, and Poisons are many of the ways to down a master of Forces. Force's potential being so grandiose makes Subtlety difficult to achieve, meaning their spells are often extremely obvious to both Mages and Sleepers.<br /> <br /> Edit: Feel free to add anything you think is mildly relevant, ask questions, or debate with someone if something seems wrong or their opinion is silly. This thread should hopefully be pretty interesting, informative and informal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 01-24-2022, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T20:47:44-08:00","id":1473136,"title":"","content":"Sorry to swiftly backtrack on the topic, but I could do with context:<br /> <br /> To what end is this being done?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T21:24:57-08:00","id":1473141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1473134-talon-survival-guide?p=1473136#post1473136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to swiftly backtrack on the topic, but I could do with context:<br /> <br /> To what end is this being done?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I have seen in a number of places (mostly reddit) people describing certain Arcana as being &quot;the combat Arcanum&quot;. This tended to happen mostly to Forces, and I failed to understand why people would describe Forces like that. I don't think of Forces as any more combat oriented in comparison to any of the other Arcana. Personally, if pressed to pick one Arcanum above all others to learn in order to win fights, I would have picked Time. I might have made a few offhand comments about that. Then I got a nice message from KaiserAfini (linked in the quote above) about Forces' combat capabilities, and I learned something (the part about enhancing your senses to empower sensory range), and figured there was plenty in all of the other Arcana that I and others could learn from. So I made the thread so I and other could learn. Then it was now. That's the context as far as I understand it and deem relevant.<br /> Edit: and I figured the AA probably has pamphlets on the subject. Hence the name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 01-24-2022, 12:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T21:44:44-08:00","id":1473142,"title":"","content":"AH. Okay. I can see how that works out.<br /> <br /> I'll need to chime in about violence with Space, because Sakura was <i>fun</i> to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T21:45:17-08:00","id":1473143,"title":"","content":"A master of Prime is a master at directly fighting other Mages. They can grind enemy spells to dust, bypass wards, and drain the mana directly from another\u2019s reserves. While true invisibility is out of their reach, a master of Prime can hide the symbols that would revel them as a enemy from those that would oppose them. They may even hide the truth of their location, so that all enemy attacks are guess. They can crush all attempts to meaningfully communicant, and weave falsehoods into truth. They can easily make symbols to draw power from.<br /> <br /> The master of Prime is always armed and armored, so long as they have mana. They may command legions of sleepwalkers and eidolons, all armed and armored with platonic forms that pierce into all forms of twilight, and any of their servants may carry imbued items allowing them to cast spells. They may thickly weave a nimbus into the battle field that their servants may be bolstered by, and their enemies hampered with the same.<br /> <br /> The entirety of the battlefield can made clear to a master of Prime, regardless of any obscurity. Neither wall, smoke, deception or twilight can hide something from the light of Truth. They need neither sound or light to sense the presence of other Mages, and can veil themselves from them.<br /> <br /> The master of Prime can cloak their spells, so that their spells do not trigger peripheral mage sight, nor readily appear to active mage sight. A master can curse you, and you would never know until it was too late.<br /> <br /> The master of Prime can afford to use mana in ventures other Mages would find too wasteful for good effect, like pattern restoration, to themselves or others, or pay off massive overreach.<br /> <br /> Its an Arcanum with clear sight, and broad applications that can mimic other arcanum, as long as you are willing to sometimes use three spells to achieve the effects of one using different arcanum.<br /> <br /> Edit: Prime\u2019s weaknesses are it\u2019s lack of direct control over things despite touching on or being able to affect many things. Prime is also not good at subtly effecting the physical Fallen World, needing other Arcana, or more spells to hide it\u2019s best spells that effect the physical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 01-24-2022, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T21:47:21-08:00","id":1473144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1473134-talon-survival-guide?p=1473142#post1473142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AH. Okay. I can see how that works out.<br /> <br /> I'll need to chime in about violence with Space, because Sakura was <i>fun</i> to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feel free. In fact, please do so, because I\u2019m extremely curious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T00:03:44-08:00","id":1473149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1473134-talon-survival-guide?p=1473141#post1473141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, if pressed to pick one Arcanum above all others to learn in order to win fights, I would have picked Time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate has a... detail where it can be used to enhance attack pools and weapon bonuses to inflict rather extreme amounts of damage readily. Cast spells on somebody else, and you can get things like causing a person to take extra from any source of damage and making several people all experience damage together.<br /> <br /> A sufficiently prepared Acanthus can fire one bullet at one person, where it just so happens to have the precision to hit them somewhere for instant death, and then five other people just go down with them.<br /> <br /> And like, use Time to go first in Initiative (mind, a boon can enhance your Initiative roll as well).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T00:25:58-08:00","id":1473151,"title":"","content":"Forces being seen as the combat Arcanum might be because it canonically is associsted with combat. It's the Arcanum of the General, and his Praetorian Ministry as well as her Prelacy of Fury.<br /> It's a highly symbolic connection, but symbolism is kind of a big deal in-setting.<br /> <br /> But practically speaking, I completely agree that Forces does not stand out from the other Arcana.<br /> When you do combat with spells, Prime is paramount for your own protection, and the warding nature of Space does a lot to build you an impenetrable fortress.<br /> If you use the Arcana to enhance mundane combat, Life should be your first choice, followed by Mind. Mind is also a great way to end combat with minimal casualties.<br /> Should you wish to attack someone's blind spot, then Spirit is great against anyone who hasn't invested in it; an army of invisible entities besetting you is difficult to deal with unless you're specifically prepared for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1473134-talon-survival-guide?p=1473143#post1473143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They may even hide the truth of their location, so that all enemy attacks are guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by this? Allowing Prime too much control over &quot;the truth of X&quot; (as opposed to truth in general) is a slippery slope of allowing Prime to do basically anything the other Arcana could do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T02:45:23-08:00","id":1473154,"title":"","content":"I think Forces is not really an Arcanum for destruction by walking up to somebody and tossing fireballs at them.<br /> <br /> It's for being able to see their gas hob from two miles away, switching it on, and then making the flame into a bonfire with the temperature of thermite that very quickly spreads to cut off the exits.<br /> <br /> That and I think some of its presumed applications are coming from some of the attitudes in its Path; some of the aspect of the wrathful deity furiously wielding the world to destroy enemies of enlightenment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 01-24-2022, 05:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T07:37:43-08:00","id":1473164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1473134-talon-survival-guide?p=1473151#post1473151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forces being seen as the combat Arcanum might be because it canonically is associsted with combat. It's the Arcanum of the General, and his Praetorian Ministry as well as her Prelacy of Fury.<br /> It's a highly symbolic connection, but symbolism is kind of a big deal in-setting.</div> </div> </div> </div> No kidding. I always thought that was because of definitions. The General is the symbol of tyranny through violence and and violence is the use of force. So the General is the Exarch of Forces.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1473134-talon-survival-guide?p=1473151#post1473151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean by this? Allowing Prime too much control over &quot;the truth of X&quot; (as opposed to truth in general) is a slippery slope of allowing Prime to do basically anything the other Arcana could do.</div> </div> </div> </div> So, I figured that ambush is one if the best tools Mages have against one another, and I asked myself how Prime would accomplish this. Hiding from PMS is a good start, but how would one hide physically with Prime? Well, what happens when one Veils the Truth? Prime has trouble affecting the physical, so it doesn\u2019t make sounds, sights or scents ie no standard illusions. On the other hand it can probably lie to Knowing spells, with a clash of wills. Secondly, it might be able to affect conclusions. (This is admittedly possibly a stretch) Let\u2019s say you veil 2+2=4 in a area, for example. You can still think 2+2=4, or say that\u2019s the solution. People can come to the \u201cwrong\u201d conclusion, and do so all the time. But it feels like it\u2019s the wrong answer. Anyone not sufficiently trained wouldn\u2019t even notice something was wrong, but anyone who has knows basic math knows the right answer. Most will probably still answer that 2+2=4, but the doubt might prevent some from answering or even have them try to guess. So by applying this to finding someone hidden, the hypothetical spell would apply a minor penalty to figuring out the location by mundane means, and lie to certain spells after winning a clash of wills. I suppose Space can do something similar, but Space would be much, much more effective at it. I\u2019m also pretty certain that Prime\u2019s thing is being able to do stuff normally exclusive to other Arcana, but worse in some way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1473134-talon-survival-guide?p=1473154#post1473154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Forces is not really an Arcanum for destruction by walking up to somebody and tossing fireballs at them.<br /> <br /> It's for being able to see their gas hob from two miles away, switching it on, and then making the flame into a bonfire with the temperature of thermite that very quickly spreads to cut off the exits.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, that is a good use of Forces, but it can be replicated by Matter and a telescope, or any of the Arcanum with access to ephemeral entities with firestarter and influence:fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1473134-talon-survival-guide?p=1473154#post1473154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That and I think some of its presumed applications are coming from some of the attitudes in its Path; some of the aspect of the wrathful deity furiously wielding the world to destroy enemies of enlightenment.</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe that\u2019s where this idea is coming from, that sounds more like a combat thing that than the Acanthus, which mostly just warns not to underestimate them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T08:01:23-08:00","id":1473166,"title":"","content":"Forces is by no means the undisputed pinnacle of combat Arcana, but it is the one that most readily lends itself to physical destruction and protection from the same. It provides the earliest access to damage dealing spells, through Control Fire and Electricity. It also more closely resembles typical combat magic from more standard fantasy rpgs. Even though slinging fireballs is a rather ill-advised application, it is an obvious one that will jump out to players and characters alike. <br /> <br /> Conversely, determining how to best use other Arcana in combat takes a bit of a mindset shift away from both traditional rpg combat and actual real-life combat. Many Arcana, like, Mind and Spirit open tactical options that simply do not exist in other contexts. As many have noted before, Supernal magic is at its most effective when it short-circuits the problem entirely, ending a fight before it can even really start. All of the Arcana can pull this off with a little creativity, including Forces.<br /> <br /> An argument can be made though that Forces actually lags behind in some contexts, because it\u2019s easier to counter with mundane means than some other Arcana. It\u2019s hard to deal with Spirit-based assaults without Spirit, for example, but the physicality of Forces means it\u2019s more often subject to physical countermeasures. (Matter would have the same problem I guess.)<br /> <br /> When you break out of the d&amp;d damage-dealing mindset, Forces can still be terrifyingly effective at ending fights. Control Gravity is a favorite of mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":23730,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","user":"Scriptorian","date":". 01-24-2022, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T14:56:51-08:00","id":1473206,"title":"","content":"I believe the next topic should be Space and it's uses in combat. However, I don't know much about that. So taking a cursory look at Space, looks like it has great awareness of the physical, (Can Space see Twilight?), and Scrying makes sensory range magic quite powerful. It seems Space should be able to bypass armor from both Forces and Matter by having weapons and such phase through the boundaries, though I am uncertain as to what Practice that falls under or if it's a reach effect of Break Boundary. Veiling Location could replicate classic d&amp;d spells like Mirror Image and Blur, though I think that's covered by the Mage Armor. Maybe one can do things like turn a melee attack into a ranged one?<br /> <br /> Back to Forces for a second, I believe that one can make &quot;cameras&quot; by using Forces Knowing? to know the light and sound that interacts with the spells subject. Has interesting implications for defense.<br /> <br /> (Also not relevant but my phone ate this post thrice. I'm rather upset about this.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T15:35:17-08:00","id":1473211,"title":"","content":"I did write a Time Weaving spell that grants autofire to melee attacks, and a Space Weaving spell that make melee attacks ranged, for the Brotherhood of the Demon Wind Legacy some time ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T15:47:12-08:00","id":1473212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1473134-talon-survival-guide?p=1473211#post1473211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did write a Time Weaving spell that grants autofire to melee attacks, and a Space Weaving spell that make melee attacks ranged, for the Brotherhood of the Demon Wind Legacy some time ago.</div> </div> </div> </div> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e?p=1053502#post1053502\">Noted</a>. Looks like it\u2019s weaving then.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T16:21:43-08:00","id":1473214,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Strategic Arcanum Dossier: Time</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;All things it devours;</span></span></span></i><br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Birds, beasts, trees, flowers;</span></span></span></i><br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Gnaws iron, bites steel;</span></span></span></i><br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Grinds hard stones to meal;</span></span></span></i><br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Slays king, ruins town,</span></span></span></i><br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And beats mountain down.&quot;</span></span></span></i><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">- Gollum describing Time</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Overview:</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The effectiveness of a mage in combat is geometrically proportional to how much time they have to prepare. A mage who had time to ready themselves can face down demigods, but one caught unaware is slightly more durable than a Sleeper. A Talon that has truly mastered Time has adapted away such a weakness.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Time is far more than speed, prophecy or even time travel. Time is how we frame reality. It is how we present the tale currently on stage, how we set the cues for the actors and props, it informs when they can imprint their intent upon the theater of life and how the story changes because of it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The sign of true mastery is to be able to break the opponent's tempo, to frame their choices in such a way that their rhythm becomes subsumed into your own and they walk unknowingly towards checkmate.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Infiltration Methods:</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When attempting to infiltrate an organization, Veiling one's past entirely can provide one with Anonymity from investigators and even make one nearly Untouchable by all but the most skilled detectives. Alternatively, utilizing the Practice to falsify it can also be remarkably effective, allowing one to create fully fleshed out Alternative Identities that can be adopted and discarded without leaving a paper trail.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This can be supplemented by utilizing divinatory and prophetic spells, tailoring interactions to win over key allies and isolate dangerous adversaries. In doing so, the future battle can be engaged in one's own terms.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When providing an alibi, Veiling one's present can allow one to move unheard and invisible through the most heavily guarded areas. Some might prefer to use a variation of temporal invisibility that leaves a looping temporal echo, providing a useful alibi.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">By choosing what conditions are required for the timeline to interact with the mage (but not the other way around), one can selectively phase through even the most heavily trapped battlefields and fortifications.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Finally, new Talons should not underestimate the utility of the <i>Veil of Moments</i>. It is more helpful than merely buying time to get emergency aid. It can allow one to continue operating at peak condition without need of food, sleep, rest or even breath. It can also allow one to survive in extreme environments without proper gear, such as a tundra, infernos or even underwater (although threats such as fire or high water pressure are as deadly as ever). This can both allow for new avenues to infiltrate compounds and provide breathing room when cut off behind enemy lines.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Preparation Logistics:</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Time is an Arcanum that lends itself well to a mage of a strategic persuasion. The most elementary application is by using divinations and prophecies to reinforce one's plans. While extremely potent, over reliance can lead to defeat via adversaries spreading temporal misinformation. Many otherwise skilled mages get so caught up in Prophecy Wars that they blundered where good deductive reasoning and common sense would have served them better. Remember always: Adaptability Is Strength.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Any Talons that wish to serve with research facilities (Athaneum, Lorehouses, Censorea, Research Bunkers, etc) should follow one important rule: as soon as whatever item you are transporting is within your sights, you temporaly lock it down immediately. Until your package arrives at a secure facility, it is liable to temporal rewriting and even the smallest vulnerability window is enough to do damage.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Teleportation remains an ever present security risk, but thankfully there is a hybrid solution from this, leveraging some fundamentals of Fate. Utilizing Fate's ability to detect sympathetic connections and destined alterations to an object, a mage can make it so it so its temporaly stuttered whenever the connection is tapped. This makes an item and its connection vanish before it is scried, teleported or similar. This has been a source of great amazement, confusion and annoyance to many a Space mage. However, due to how blatant this effect is, it requires additional preparation so as to not trigger The Curse. Additional Veiling spellwork or an isolated facility tend to suffice.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The ability to quickly alter and redefine the battlefield remains as one of Time's strongest assets. By Unmaking the required intervals to execute actions, a mage can prepare multiple mundane solutions. Entire fortifications can be completed in less than a minute, equipment construction, customization and research can be completed in an irrisory interval. A few of the Arrow's high end research facilities have completed centuries worth of research in days, thus combat exoskeletons and mech suits have become available for world ending emergencies.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Whenever the battlefield is known, masters of Time can Make large time pockets in the area. This allows for months of planning, fortification, magical preparation and training drills to be completed in seconds. Precarious situations can thus be turned to rallying victories.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Preparing contingency spells should always be a common praxis to those who know this Arcanum. Emergency teleportations, Twilight gates, flight and healing are common ones.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The careful and deliberate application of Hung Spells and similar effects can make all the difference in the battle, by allowing powerful spells to be prepared. Some prefer the variation that encodes the Imago into beads of possibility, making portable spells. A few alter the Imago as it enters the Fallen World, making AoE spells that follow a central target. All of these contribute to the toolkit a strategist may employ.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Against very complex situations, a mage can summon potential selves to be at multiple places at once and wield their full spellcasting might. However, caster should be aware that they do not diverge the history of their Awakened self, thus all are tapping from the same spell control pool. Thus judicious management of their collective resources is key to success.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Defensive Measures:</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The first and most fundamental law of using this Arcanum strategically: if its something important your cabal is discussing, Shield it from temporal senses. Ideally you would want a combination with Veiling. First attempt to misdirect the enemy with bad information, for the strategic gains are significant. Should that fail, the second layer should blatantly defend your plans from scrutiny.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When facing a difficult foe or requiring to recover a target alive, a subject can be Stunned by Weaving the conditions that allow them to interact with the timeline (but not the reverse). Thus they can be transported safely, since breaking away without supernatural abilities is utterly impossible.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Within an active battlefield, Acceleration's ability to provide rapid movement and facilitate dodging should not be overlooked. Sometimes its best used as a distraction, with a mage keeping a werewolf busy as his cabalmates ready the spell to complete the mission. The ability to predict the enemy's next move can be invaluable, thus a prophetic analysis of the adversary allows one to make the most effective move at the most efficient time. Both approaches allow the mage to act at the optimal moment, interrupting devastating attacks, amplifying their tactical flexibility.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Some mages prefer to use a type of light combat divination, allowing them to adjust their position while wasting no movement. This way they can choose to benefit from traditional defenses or dodge using the minimal motions, even while carrying out devastating attacks.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In truly dire situations, some Talons choose to give themselves the capability of receiving only positive changes. This allows them to walk through lava or across a hail of bullets with no fear. While supernatural phenomena will still attempt to wrestle against their will to cause damage, the sheer benefit of this method makes it a powerful aegis. It can also be used to create indestructible walls and protect valuable cargo.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">No defensive debriefing would be complete without extolling the utility of <i>Time Heal</i>. So long as there is still life in the subject and the damage isn't so fundamental to their Pattern as to resist magical healing, then they can be saved. Fully healing someone of any damage without consuming mana means it can be a lifeline when resources are running out.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Offensive Tactics:</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When situations start to escalate, sometimes all that is needed to force a surrender are precise strikes. No matter how charged with magic, at the end of the day, imbued and enhanced items are mundane on nature. Time is able to bypass their durability, armor piercing ability and potentially wither them to dust. Suddenly reducing a firing squad to fighting bare handed sends a powerful message, the same can be said of melee fighters or mages that are over reliant on magical trinkets. Similarly, the judicious application of structural damage can cut off certain sections of a building or tunnel, allowing for either an expeditious retreat or an offensive relying on defeat by detail.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">When confronting foes directly, equipment can be enchanted to provide automatic fire to a multitude of weapons, simultaneously increasing the efficiency of reloading and positioning. Pistols and sniper rifles are common targets, but missile and grenade launchers also prove highly effective. Some mages prefer chainsaws, for the sheer shock value of seeing such a devastating weapon wielding more swiftly than any blade. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Some prefer throwing daggers, bows, crossbows and even boomerangs, favoring the silence and precision they bring. Boosted speed and evasive ability have been combined with this to great success, using the tension of quiet assaults and baiting tactics to destabilize the enemy, allowing for a modern reinterpretation of the Mongolian harrying and ambushing tactic.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lastly, a master of Time should be mindful that every battlefield is a resource. The alleyway where werewolves fought a mummy last week, the warehouse where two master mages tried to kill each other, the condemned hotel where rival gangs fought last night. All it takes is a Making to create a parallel timeline, with but some nudging from the purview of change, they can be summoned forth and see the mage's foes as their enemies. Seize the edge of history and wield it as the blade of the Adamantine Way.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 02-12-2022, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T18:17:31-08:00","id":1473218,"title":"","content":"Thoughts on Space: Inward and Outward Eye combines really well with Nightvision. Scrying and Sympathetic range open up a number of possibilities (which in turn makes Wards desirable). But Ban is one of my favorite spells. Cast it on yourself to get protection while you prepare shenanigans. Cast it on an enemy to take them out of the fight. Cast it on your friend the rampaging werewolf/vampire to put them in timeout. Cast it on an area to contain hazards. Tis a fun and versatile spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T18:26:40-08:00","id":1473219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1473134-talon-survival-guide?p=1473218#post1473218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts on Space: Inward and Outward Eye combines really well with Nightvision. Scrying and Sympathetic range open up a number of possibilities (which in turn makes Wards desirable). But Ban is one of my favorite spells. Cast it on yourself to get protection while you prepare shenanigans. Cast it on an enemy to take them out of the fight. Cast it on your friend the rampaging werewolf/vampire to put them in timeout. Cast it on an area to contain hazards. Tis a fun and versatile spell.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Make a ban that affects all non-human mage supernatural minds. Suddenly the fierce werewolves that charge in with spirits in tow get placed in a vegetative state. Next time they might be much more inclined to a diplomatic solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T18:42:34-08:00","id":1473221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1473134-talon-survival-guide?p=1473219#post1473219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Make a ban that affects all non-human mage supernatural minds. Suddenly the fierce werewolves that charge in with spirits in tow get placed in a vegetative state. Next time they might be much more inclined to a diplomatic solution.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u2026does that particular interaction work like that though? I thought Ban acted as if there was no Space in the aoe for the Banned things. Shouldn\u2019t the Banned minds cause the body to pass through the other side, since the body is connected to the mind, or force a astral projection rather than temporarily suppress the mind?<br /> <br /> Edit: By the way I love everyone\u2019s posts so far!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T18:53:19-08:00","id":1473222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1473134-talon-survival-guide?p=1473221#post1473221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u2026does that particular interaction work like that though? I thought Ban acted as if there was no Space in the aoe for the Banned things. Shouldn\u2019t the Banned minds cause the body to pass through the other side, since the body is connected to the mind, or force a astral projection rather than temporarily suppress the mind?<br /> <br /> Edit: By the way I love everyone\u2019s posts so far!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It would probably astrally project them Dr Strange style. There is this really good AP called <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/mage-the-awakening-the-voice-of-freedom.408237/\" target=\"_blank\">The Voice of Freedom</a> where one PC does exactly that, making the werewolves go from boisterous to &quot;I think that one might be a Lovecraftian horror in human form, why don't we tone down the aggression ?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T18:54:20-08:00","id":1473223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1473134-talon-survival-guide?p=1473219#post1473219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Make a ban that affects all non-human mage supernatural minds. Suddenly the fierce werewolves that charge in with spirits in tow get placed in a vegetative state. Next time they might be much more inclined to a diplomatic solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect this would be a separate spell from Ban \u2014 \u201cyou shall not enter\u201d and \u201cyou shall sleep\u201d seem too far away, symbolically speaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T19:03:27-08:00","id":1473224,"title":"","content":"Let\u2019s say we play with Matter and Ban, do you think people would notice weapons leaving holsters and stuff if we Ban weapons? Oh, wait, is it possible to modify Ban so that Banned things end up at another location of the casters choice, instead of passing through?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T20:14:01-08:00","id":1473227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1473134-talon-survival-guide?p=1473224#post1473224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let\u2019s say we play with Matter and Ban, do you think people would notice weapons leaving holsters and stuff if we Ban weapons? Oh, wait, is it possible to modify Ban so that Banned things end up at another location of the casters choice, instead of passing through?</div> </div> </div> </div>By combining with Co-Location or Teleportation, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T22:18:42-08:00","id":1473235,"title":"","content":"One unusual thing that Space can do, should the mage not care to be covert, is to increase their size. That means that they get more health and are much harder to hit with scale factors. It also means more targeted attacks (since perhaps they can only hit one limb) and more chaos on the battlefield via area of effect spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-25-2022, 01:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T06:13:23-08:00","id":1473252,"title":"","content":"Mind you, the Adamantine Arrow as written in the Order book have standards for using magic fairly sparingly. If you're not able to overcome obstacles that don't severely outclass you or have a deeply supernatural element with just natural skills slightly enhanced by spells, then you're not sufficiently challenging or honing yourself, and you won't learn anything from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T08:57:49-08:00","id":1473266,"title":"","content":"Good luck trying to engage directly with Enchanters. Actually, poor choice of words there, sorry. You're not going to have good luck. With their Ruling Arcana, they'll spot you coming the moment you formulate a plan of attack. They were always just here a few minutes ago, always just around the corner, right in the next room, keep going, you're almost there. They'll make it so you have to go on a quest to gather the like seven crystals of Rem Lezar before you can even think about approaching their Sanctum. Accept that the fight will be under their terms and conditions, that your every move will bring a new flavor of curse, a new rule to follow or forfeit, another oath sworn. (&quot;You didn't read the sign out front that stepping on the blue tile means you agree not to cast Unmaking spells on pain of losing an arm? It was plain as day! Maybe you need to brush up on your Old Burmese. . .&quot;) Sometimes the unscrupulous ones will foist a Destiny on some poor sap to fight you in their stead (or even worse, a Doom). Strategy? That's a kind of intent, isn't it? How do you effectively fight someone who can change what you're fighting over mid-battle?<br /> <br /> Overwhelming force and unpredictability, most likely. Striking fast and decisively means less risk of getting bogged down in Acanthus bullshit. (Arrow Caucuses may be the only place where the concept of a &quot;preemptive defensive attack&quot; is genuinely justifiable.) In the old tales, it's usually another fairy who manages to undo or at least lighten the curse levied by one of the fae, and having a Witch of your own on your side can work wonders to even the playing field, hexes and boons cancelling each other out in a side-game of prophecy-tag, so long as you understand that you are absolutely being used as a pawn in some greater conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T10:27:52-08:00","id":1473276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1473134-talon-survival-guide?p=1473266#post1473266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good luck trying to engage directly with Enchanters. Actually, poor choice of words there, sorry. You're not going to have good luck. With their Ruling Arcana, they'll spot you coming the moment you formulate a plan of attack. They were always just here a few minutes ago, always just around the corner, right in the next room, keep going, you're almost there. They'll make it so you have to go on a quest to gather the like seven crystals of Rem Lezar before you can even think about approaching their Sanctum. Accept that the fight will be under their terms and conditions, that your every move will bring a new flavor of curse, a new rule to follow or forfeit, another oath sworn. (&quot;You didn't read the sign out front that stepping on the blue tile means you agree not to cast Unmaking spells on pain of losing an arm? It was plain as day! Maybe you need to brush up on your Old Burmese. . .&quot;) Sometimes the unscrupulous ones will foist a Destiny on some poor sap to fight you in their stead (or even worse, a Doom). Strategy? That's a kind of intent, isn't it? How do you effectively fight someone who can change what you're fighting over mid-battle?<br /> <br /> Overwhelming force and unpredictability, most likely. Striking fast and decisively means less risk of getting bogged down in Acanthus bullshit. (Arrow Caucuses may be the only place where the concept of a &quot;preemptive defensive attack&quot; is genuinely justifiable.) In the old tales, it's usually another fairy who manages to undo or at least lighten the curse levied by one of the fae, and having a Witch of your own on your side can work wonders to even the playing field, hexes and boons cancelling each other out in a side-game of prophecy-tag, so long as you understand that you are absolutely being used as a pawn in some greater conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lets see, Sworn Oaths says:<br /> <br /> <i>No one can be forced to take such an oath, although a subject may be placed under oath unwittingly if he voluntarily makes a vow and verbally agrees to a specified consequence, even if he doesn\u2019t realize the mage can enforce the oath supernaturally</i><br /> <br /> So it seems like the blue tile option counts as voluntarily (if unknowingly), making a vow. But as brilliant as such a &quot;fae legalese&quot; trap is, I am not sure if it could be enforced without verbal agreement.<br /> <br /> However, that spell is specifically designed for oral contracts. I think variations to other symbolic ones also apply, such as written contracts and social contracts (crossing the pomerium as an ancient Roman, club rules, etc). Its arguable that if the rules are available in some explicit form (which the contractor may not fully understand), then tricking them into agreement is symbolically aligned with the Fae (plus its overall very thematic).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 01-27-2022, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T11:52:05-08:00","id":1473291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1473134-talon-survival-guide?p=1473252#post1473252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, the Adamantine Arrow as written in the Order book have standards for using magic fairly sparingly. If you're not able to overcome obstacles that don't severely outclass you or have a deeply supernatural element with just natural skills slightly enhanced by spells, then you're not sufficiently challenging or honing yourself, and you won't learn anything from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure the relevance of this in a thread explicitly about the Arcana as combat/violence tools that just happens to have the Adamantine Arrow reference in the title as a cheeky way about conveying that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T01:27:19-08:00","id":1473453,"title":"","content":"Just responding to the opening comments on forces.<br /> <br /> A Master of Life can fly, simply Patterning into the body of a bird, better still an Eagle eyed mage can now use sensory range comparable to the forces master. Weaving into her pattern camouflage and natural armour gives stealth and protection. Combined with sonar for echo location and electroception her sensory range can be expanded far beyond human capability; even a blank spot not echoing any sound would be detectable to echo location (if they have merely stopped sound rather than redirecting it around themselves).<br /> <br /> For blunt offensive effects, the Master of Life is limited to living beings, with difficulty directly targeting Golems, Eidolon and possibly Zombies along with Spirits, Ghosts, and Goetia. However so long as their target has a living body they can directly Fray the pattern. Can inflivt poison, blindness, or deafness. She can cause arm racks or immobilisation (very useful for non lethal effects), or remove the target from combat by triggering its flight responce or making it fall asleep (or possibly reduce your dexterity to the point where you can't move?)<br /> <br /> Some of the larger scale effects require a bit more subtlety, Making a new disease which will spread among multiple people (and possibly follow you while you retreat).<br /> <br /> Lastly their ability to Know life patterns gives them vital intelligence when it comes to how much damage is necessary to kill/incapacitate each target. She can prioritse who to attack and with carefully controlled potency not kill targets who need to be taken alive.<br /> <br /> And that is all assuming you want to directly compete with the Forces Master style of magical violence from the opening. <br /> <br /> Another Master of Life might just aswell sneak around as a tiny animal, or fly overhead as a Robin, before shapeshifting into an armoured Bear and landing directly on the target to quickly rip them apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-28-2022, 06:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T02:07:20-08:00","id":1473454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1473134-talon-survival-guide?p=1473206#post1473206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the next topic should be Space and it's uses in combat. However, I don't know much about that. So taking a cursory look at Space, looks like it has great awareness of the physical, (Can Space see Twilight?), and Scrying makes sensory range magic quite powerful. It seems Space should be able to bypass armor from both Forces and Matter by having weapons and such phase through the boundaries, though I am uncertain as to what Practice that falls under or if it's a reach effect of Break Boundary. Veiling Location could replicate classic d&amp;d spells like Mirror Image and Blur, though I think that's covered by the Mage Armor. Maybe one can do things like turn a melee attack into a ranged one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Space has (at least) one extremely effective combat option, with 2 extra reach, Co-location allows the Master of Space appear reflecively, attack and then disappear reflecively. Basically blinking in and out without giving anyone a chance to respond.<br /> <br /> The spell can be keyed to allow allies with some space do the same while preventing enemies from taking advantage of their spell. <br /> <br /> They can potentially do this from a sanctum, making retreat to a safe (possibly warded) location trivial, while also having easy access to all the resources of that location to use in the fight if needed.<br /> <br /> But even without a sanctum, they can walk up behind someone and (potentially) push their weapons or armour across, effectively Teleporting away their equipment. If the target can see them (requiring they have some space magic, or an extra reach from the Master) she can act as a distraction, impervious to attacks while able to reflecively attack and return to intangiblity.<br /> <br /> The only downside of this Co-location is it is very easy for the enemy to retreat** out of the area it covers (if they know how large it is), forcing the Master to recast it. But allowing her to secure a vital location. Perhaps removing hostages, artifacts, or other mission critical objects <br /> <br /> This one spell makes a Master of Space extremely useful in a fight.<br /> <br /> In a far more subtle sense, she can manipulate the strong sympathetic connections to reduce an enemy group's bonds. Can learn what is important to any given target and threaten it to further undermine group cohesion, or strengthen connections to make each member of a group care about different (perhaps competing) interests. <br /> <br /> Undermining group cohesion before a fight even becomes necessary can grant victory before you even start.<br /> <br /> Lastly, Perfect Sympathy gives a unique ability to redirect spells cast on the Master of Space at sympathic range to a different target (Clash of Wills required) - though the ability to cast lasting destruction of sympathic connections after the fact is already there.<br /> <br /> EDIT: space can NOT see twilight, because it isn't a space (it is a state of being). Though co-locate can make the Master of Space appear intangible (as if they were in twilight), it is a different effect entirel (ie they are completely tangible on their side of the Co-location).<br /> <br /> Scrying requires a sympathic connection, usually, i suppose you can cast a scrying window on something you can sense, and then walk off/teleport home. <br /> <br /> I don't think break boundaries can bypass armour, though it can breach panic rooms and similar. <br /> <br /> Not sure about melee attacks becoming ranged.<br /> <br /> **EDIT2: i should also mention, leaving an area which a Master of Space doesn't want you to leave may not be as easy as i made put above. Between a blunt Ban (which will immediately invoke attempts to dispell) and a more subtle Lying Maps/Veiling exits/alter direction, you can make labyrinthine confusion which is harder to see.<br /> <br /> Or you can go all out and Quarentine the area.<br /> <br /> EDIT3: come to think of it, a small Ban plus co-locating in some mundane fire to burn up all their oxygen will incapacitate most targets (at least those that need to breath). Much easier than actually fighting them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 01-28-2022, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}